{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "0b533efb-952f-5173-ac30-a5bc40fa5da6"/*PhysicsRopeBridgeExample*/,
  "Description": "A sagging plank bridge held by two kinematic anchors, with a crate dropped on it.\n\nNine planks are chained with ball-socket [RigidJoint] operators. The planks start on a gentle curve so the bridge hangs slack, the crate lands in the middle, bounces and slides off.\n\nAKA: chain, rope, hanging bridge, joints\n\nTips\n- Lower Frequency on the joints to make the bridge stretch more.\n- Each joint offset is half the plank spacing, in the local space of the plank it belongs to.",
